hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"19181","Yazid informed us: al-Masudi informed us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Jabir ibn Samura, from Nafi ibn Utba, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You shall fight the Arabian Peninsula and Allah shall open it, and you shall fight Persia and Allah shall open them, and you shall fight the Romans and Allah shall open them, and you shall fight the Dajjal and Allah shall open him."
"19182","Muawiya ibn Amr narrated to us: Abu Ishaq, meaning al-Fazari, narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Jabir ibn Samura, from Nafi ibn Utba, he said: I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a campaign, and people from the west came to him wearing wool garments and met him at a mound, they standing while he sat. So I came to him and stood between them and him. So I retained from him four phrases counting them in my hand. He said: You shall raid the Arabian Peninsula and Allah shall open it, then you shall raid Persia and Allah shall open it, then you shall raid the Romans and Allah shall open it, then you shall raid the Dajjal and Allah shall open him. Nafi said: O Jabir, do you not see that the Dajjal emerges only after the Romans are opened?"
